{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T21:54:51.240573Z","id":"126f9fab752608b8e5f588dfba7b2465d9c89b53a27ddf96bf36f0b707638704","body":{"detail":"`Pending::issue_registration` (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs) is given an ID, a name and a hash, so `StoredPending` writes the store's row (`Store::issue_registration`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_surfaces.rs) with `prompt: None` and `settings: null`, though the table has both. The hub holds the prompt and settings a host registered for as long as it holds the registration, and replaces them when the host registers as it again. Three things follow. (1) A run's first turn is sent the prompt its registration has now (`OutsideProvider::prompt`, crates/clax-bot/src/outside.rs, from `Served::prompt`), not the one registered when the run was bound: a host that registers another prompt changes it for runs already made that have not taken their first turn. (2) After the daemon restarts, or the registration's lease ends, the hub holds nothing until the host registers again: a run that takes its first turn then is sent the standard prompt, and its calls' deadlines are the policy's alone, since `Served::settings` is the default. (3) A step that is executed again re-reads neither: the system prompt is stored with the first turn. Passing the prompt and settings to `issue_registration` and reading them back by registration ID (and keeping the prompt beside the definition's hash the run was bound with) would close all three; it changes the hub's `Pending` trait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"034915abcc6ddbd12d01394bc5f0af10275fe6d4cfd5a02f546de240a690b877"},"summary":"A registration issued through the hub's store keeps no prompt and no settings: both live in the hub's memory, with the registration and not with a definition's hash","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T21:54:51.240664Z","id":"40eb49b1755bd9cf43157fbcc31e72f50d3451ef5ed7472dd9ee4b73344f3167","body":{"detail":"(1) `Pending::sent_calls(ids)` has no instant and `Store::mark_sent` wants one: the adapter marks the calls at the last instant any of its methods was given, which is the `serve`'s opening (`Hub::close` is given `now` but passes none on). The stamp is read only as set or not. (2) The store's pending row documents `args` as the arguments the script passed (crates/clax-store/src/bot_pending.rs, `PendingCall::args`); the adapter writes the checked arguments there (one value for each parameter, `null` for an optional one left out), because that row is what a `serve` delivers to the host, and writes the hash of the script's own arguments as `args_hash`, which is what the journal row of the place must hold. (3) `Pending::open_call` cannot be implemented over the store (a pending row is one place of one attempt under a claim): it answers the error `call_unplaced`, and only `BrokerStore::open_placed` opens calls. Also seen, and not the adapter's to change: the store stops a call's wait when its step commits without it, where `MemoryPending` holds the call until its deadline (`outside::waiting` asserts each), and ends kept at one instant are listed in the order of their runs' IDs (`outside::conformance` sorts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"b0dc48f26eaad5991bbaff8e7577e06785bd2ff0dbb31ec7cf530515a82238ab"},"summary":"Three places where the hub's `Pending` and the store's functions do not meet exactly, and what the adapter does at each","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T22:09:01.227324Z","id":"8d7a9577ebb2ae7170d09cf2cafaf28c60a262d3dbeca3421bbd68430b846dfc","body":{"detail":"`StoredPending::act_with(ctx, person, prompt, settings)` sets what `issue_registration` writes, and the route (crates/clax-http/src/bot_surfaces.rs `Surfaces::register`) gives it the request's and clears it after (test: api_bot_surfaces.rs a_surface_registers_in_either_notation_and_is_listed reads the row). Still open: (1) a host that registers again as its ID sends its prompt and settings again, which the hub then holds, but the row keeps the first ones: clax-store has no function that changes a registration's row; (2) `CallBroker::registration` for a registration the hub does not hold still answers default settings and no prompt, though the row now has what it was made with; (3) a run is still sent the prompt its registration has when it takes its first turn.","kind":"comment","references":"126f9fab752608b8e5f588dfba7b2465d9c89b53a27ddf96bf36f0b707638704","summary":"Part done: the store's row now keeps the prompt file and settings a registration was first made with; what a resumed or unheld registration reads is unchanged","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:02.802335Z","id":"c0bba3111cd00642d0a1e7b65c000da99fd92f20524726d82f4e56248271b99e","body":{"detail":"`Pending::issue_registration` (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs) is given an ID, a name and a hash, so `StoredPending` writes the store's row (`Store::issue_registration`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_surfaces.rs) with `prompt: None` and `settings: null`, though the table has both. The hub holds the prompt and settings a host registered for as long as it holds the registration, and replaces them when the host registers as it again. Three things follow. (1) A run's first turn is sent the prompt its registration has now (`OutsideProvider::prompt`, crates/clax-bot/src/outside.rs, from `Served::prompt`), not the one registered when the run was bound: a host that registers another prompt changes it for runs already made that have not taken their first turn. (2) After the daemon restarts, or the registration's lease ends, the hub holds nothing until the host registers again: a run that takes its first turn then is sent the standard prompt, and its calls' deadlines are the policy's alone, since `Served::settings` is the default. (3) A step that is executed again re-reads neither: the system prompt is stored with the first turn. Passing the prompt and settings to `issue_registration` and reading them back by registration ID (and keeping the prompt beside the definition's hash the run was bound with) would close all three; it changes the hub's `Pending` trait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":243},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"0c33edbccccd4ab0fe8f32c23142138b01c623db5c7b8551d7d823f2dae0d2ae"},"summary":"A registration issued through the hub's store keeps no prompt and no settings: both live in the hub's memory, with the registration and not with a definition's hash","supersedes":"126f9fab752608b8e5f588dfba7b2465d9c89b53a27ddf96bf36f0b707638704","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:02.973361Z","id":"8142ad65c31e447609babb710592afb733500bd722497305731cdf6314fe8c14","body":{"detail":"(1) `Pending::sent_calls(ids)` has no instant and `Store::mark_sent` wants one: the adapter marks the calls at the last instant any of its methods was given, which is the `serve`'s opening (`Hub::close` is given `now` but passes none on). The stamp is read only as set or not. (2) The store's pending row documents `args` as the arguments the script passed (crates/clax-store/src/bot_pending.rs, `PendingCall::args`); the adapter writes the checked arguments there (one value for each parameter, `null` for an optional one left out), because that row is what a `serve` delivers to the host, and writes the hash of the script's own arguments as `args_hash`, which is what the journal row of the place must hold. (3) `Pending::open_call` cannot be implemented over the store (a pending row is one place of one attempt under a claim): it answers the error `call_unplaced`, and only `BrokerStore::open_placed` opens calls. Also seen, and not the adapter's to change: the store stops a call's wait when its step commits without it, where `MemoryPending` holds the call until its deadline (`outside::waiting` asserts each), and ends kept at one instant are listed in the order of their runs' IDs (`outside::conformance` sorts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":351},"end":{"line":353},"content_hash":"b0dc48f26eaad5991bbaff8e7577e06785bd2ff0dbb31ec7cf530515a82238ab"},"summary":"Three places where the hub's `Pending` and the store's functions do not meet exactly, and what the adapter does at each","supersedes":"40eb49b1755bd9cf43157fbcc31e72f50d3451ef5ed7472dd9ee4b73344f3167","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T01:14:37.073177Z","id":"fccc59ea46637e68a121c251dcc6bc5f9f498596f6d2b3f549d54814e5f3a7fd","body":{"detail":"Of the three things the record lists: (1) is closed: a run's binding names the SHA-256 of the prompt file its registration had when the run was started, and its first turn is sent the text kept under that hash (`OutsideProvider::prompt`, crates/clax-bot/src/outside.rs), so registering another prompt changes it for runs started afterwards alone. (2), the prompt half: a run whose registration is not held (the daemon restarted, the lease ended) is sent its own prompt file, read from `bot_surface_prompts` by hash; test `outside::prompt::in_the_store` (crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs) drives such a run over a new hub on the same store. (2), the settings half, is unchanged and is what still wants a decision: `CallBroker::registration` (crates/clax-bot/src/broker.rs) answers `Settings::default()` for a registration the hub does not hold, though the row has the settings it was last gone on with (`Registration::settings`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_surfaces.rs), so such a run's calls have the policy's deadlines alone; and a held registration's settings are its current ones, not those the run was started under. (3) stands as it was: the system prompt is stored with the first turn. The registration's row now names its prompt file by hash (`bot_registrations.prompt_hash`), and `Registration::prompt` reads the text through it.","kind":"comment","references":"126f9fab752608b8e5f588dfba7b2465d9c89b53a27ddf96bf36f0b707638704","summary":"Built for the prompt: a run keeps the prompt file it was started with, by hash, also over a restart. Still open: an unheld registration's settings read as the defaults","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/broker/stored.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:11:15.916967Z","id":"2b7634bdd9c3dee2181961e358d7d36afacea84734b64a3716eb945bc5af8513","body":{"detail":"Pending::registration_settings (crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs; StoredPending reads Store::registration(id).settings) is what HubBroker::registration answers as Served::settings for an unheld registration, in place of Settings::default(). Test: crates/clax-bot/tests/outside.rs kept_settings::in_the_store (a new hub over the same store: the provider's settings are the row's; a run started under call_timeout_s 5 is sent its call with expires_in_ms 5000 after its host goes on with no settings). Of the record's three parts, (1) and (2) are now built for prompt and settings; (3) stands. Proposed close for the owner.","kind":"comment","references":"c0bba3111cd00642d0a1e7b65c000da99fd92f20524726d82f4e56248271b99e","summary":"The settings half is built (38fd548bd): a run reads the settings its binding keeps, and a binding that keeps none reads the registration's row while the hub does not hold it","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
